      "reply": "Here is the re-pitch, in simpler words and with the terms from `GLOSSARY.md`.\n\n**Context:** your question was how the task continues after you approve it.\n\n**Answer:**\n\nWhen you approve the task, the Graph stops at a point where it waits for your confirmation. At that point, the Graph saves a Checkpoint.\n\nThe Checkpoint links your approval to the task execution that is on hold. So the Graph can continue the same execution later.\n\nAfter the Graph starts again, the next Node writes the report.\n\nOne limit is important. A Checkpoint does not guarantee that an external action happens only once. If the system stops unexpectedly, a write to an external file can happen a second time. So this design is not an exactly-once guarantee for a file write after a crash.",
